<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-10.25%" pitch="-2.25%">
      A lawyer stood up to test Jesus.<break time="500ms"/>
      He was a man who knew the law well, who had studied it, who lived inside its questions.<break time="500ms"/>
      He asked: Teacher, what shall I do to inherit eternal life?<break time="1000ms"/>
      It was not an idle question, even if the motive behind it was testing.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Jesus answered a question with a question.<break time="500ms"/>
      What is written in the law? What do you read there?<break time="1000ms"/>
      The lawyer answered from memory and from conviction.<break time="1800ms"/>

      You shall love the Lord your God with all your heart and with all your soul.<break time="500ms"/>
      And with all your strength and with all your mind.<break time="500ms"/>
      And your neighbor as yourself.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Two commandments, woven together into one answer.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Jesus said: you have answered correctly.<break time="500ms"/>
      Do this, and you will live.<break time="1000ms"/>
      The answer was already there, complete and clear.<break time="1800ms"/>

      But the lawyer, desiring to justify himself, asked a further question.<break time="500ms"/>
      And who is my neighbor?<break time="1000ms"/>
      It is a question that sounds like it is about definition.<break time="500ms"/>
      About limits, about lines, about who qualifies.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Jesus did not answer with a definition.<break time="500ms"/>
      He answered with a story.<break time="500ms"/>
      He placed the question on a road and let it walk.<break time="1000ms"/>
      He showed what the answer looks like when it moves.<break time="1800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
